## ruby#400: a text capture over a reference-built rule stays the
## matched text under edition 2. The capture spans the rules it
## references, so their bodies compile unwrapped and the capture's
## value equals its edition-1 shape — edition 2 stays purely additive.
grammar CaptureOverReference version "1.0.0" edition "v2" {
  root = number as num
  number = 1*digit
  digit = %x30-39
  entry main: root

  test {
    accept "123"
    capture "123" { num: "123" }
    reject "12a"
  }
}
